Package: belgian-azerty-windows
Architecture: all
Depends: xkb-data, keyboard-configuration, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: keyd-belgian-windows, libglib2.0-bin, zenity, pkexec
Description: Belgian AZERTY keyboard that behaves like on Windows
 The Belgian layout on Linux is correct, but a few Windows habits are
 missing. This package provides them for Ubuntu-based systems such as
 Linux Mint and Zorin OS:
 .
  * the XKB option caps:be_windows: Caps Lock gives the Shift level on the
    whole main block (digits row and punctuation), as Windows "Belgian
    (Period)" and "Belgian (Comma)" do; ², <, AltGr and the numpad are
    unaffected;
  * be-azerty-fix, which makes every place that stores the keyboard layout
    (console, boot prompt, login screen, desktop, defaults for new users)
    agree on Belgian, with the Period or Comma numpad, and can undo it all.
 .
 Installing the package only makes the Caps Lock option available; run
 "sudo be-azerty-fix system" to switch it on. The Ctrl+Alt = AltGr habit is
 in the keyd-belgian-windows package.
